From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperLeiyan <SuperLeiyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 57/57] PC5: a game a home screen tile started has no close
 combo

Touchpad and Options held for two seconds closed the game and went back to
PC5's screens; started from a tile (exit_after), it closed to the home
screen. A tile is an app of its own, closed as any app is, from the game's
own menu or from the home screen, so in a game a tile started the combo
does nothing. Every other game keeps it.
---
 native/wine64_main.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/native/wine64_main.c b/native/wine64_main.c
index 034bdb1..aeca653 100644
--- a/native/wine64_main.c
+++ b/native/wine64_main.c
@@ -2027,8 +2027,10 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
         if (pad_status == PW_OK && (pad.core.pressed_edges & PAD_CREATE) &&
             !(pad.core.previous_buttons & PAD_OPTIONS))
             PS5LOG_LOG("PW_WINE64 marker by=player tick=%llu", (unsigned long long)tick);
-        combo_ticks = pad_status == PW_OK && (pad.core.previous_buttons & PAD_CLOSE) == PAD_CLOSE ?
-                      combo_ticks + 1 : 0;
+        /* A game a home screen tile started is closed as any app is, from its own menu or the
+         * home screen: the combo is the screens' way back, and a tile has none. */
+        combo_ticks = pad_status == PW_OK && !launch.exit_after &&
+                      (pad.core.previous_buttons & PAD_CLOSE) == PAD_CLOSE ? combo_ticks + 1 : 0;
         if (!close_requested &&
             (combo_ticks >= PW_WINE64_CLOSE_HOLD_TICKS ||
              (PW_WINE64_SECONDS && now - started >= (uint64_t)PW_WINE64_SECONDS * 1000000000u))) {
